IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wra4-regulative`

-- Traces of the regulative rules of wra4-regulative.l4. A #TRACE prints its outcome; check.sh does not count it, and the stable
-- binary cannot #ASSERT on a DEONTIC (see NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept"). The outcome expected is
-- written beside each trace, and the twin decision functions carry the asserted tests.

-- s 96A(1): review within 1826 days of the last review. Reviewing on day 1000: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 96A(1) the duty to review the sums` 1826 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 96A(1) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 96A(1) review the sums specified in section 96(5A)` AT 1000
-- Expected: FULFILLED

-- Reviewing on day 1826, the last day: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 96A(1) the duty to review the sums` 1826 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 96A(1) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 96A(1) review the sums specified in section 96(5A)` AT 1826
-- Expected: FULFILLED

-- Reviewing on day 1827, after the period: BREACH.
#TRACE `s 96A(1) the duty to review the sums` 1826 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 96A(1) the Secretary of State` DOES `s 96A(1) review the sums specified in section 96(5A)` AT 1827
-- Expected: BREACH

-- s 115(2): withdrawing on day 14: FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 115(2) the permission to withdraw the agreement` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 115(2) the person who agreed to pay the penalty` DOES `s 115(2) withdraw the agreement` AT 14
-- Expected: FULFILLED

-- s 127(5): without the authority, onward supply on day 3 is a breach.
#TRACE `s 127(5) the prohibition on onward supply` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 127(5) the recipient of the information` DOES `s 127(5) supply the information to any other person or body` AT 3
-- Expected: BREACH

-- s 127(5): with the authority, the same onward supply is not a breach.
#TRACE `s 127(5) the prohibition on onward supply` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 127(5) the recipient of the information` DOES `s 127(5) supply the information to any other person or body` AT 3
-- Expected: FULFILLED

-- s 129(1): where the bar applies, disclosure on day 2 is a breach.
#TRACE `s 129(1) the prohibition on disclosure` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 129(1) the person to whom the information is supplied, or an employee or former employee of that person` DOES `s 129(1) disclose the information` AT 2
-- Expected: BREACH

-- s 129(1): where an exception removes the bar, the same disclosure is not a breach.
#TRACE `s 129(1) the prohibition on disclosure` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 129(1) the person to whom the information is supplied, or an employee or former employee of that person` DOES `s 129(1) disclose the information` AT 2
-- Expected: FULFILLED
